@startuml emergency-stop
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Emergency stop: task-board emergency-stop (estop), proposed

actor "Operator" as P $PERSON
participant "task-board emergency-stop" as E $SERVICE
participant "task-board kernel\n(task-board's own code,\nno model)" as K $SERVICE
participant "Session host" as H $SERVICE
participant "Orchestrator sessions" as S $AGENT
participant "Runs" as R $AGENT
database "Boards" as B $COMMITTED

P -> E: estop [--process NAME]
E -> P: lists every session and run it will stop;\n"type STOP to continue"
P -> E: STOP
note right of E
  refused from inside a hosted
  session or a run (operator only)
end note
E -> K: snapshot every affected board
K -> B: runs in flight, Change Requests awaiting\nreview or integration, obligations, unrouted notices
E -> H: interrupt: write a short note (10-30 s, default 20)
H -> S: interrupt, then the note request
S -> B: optional short note
E -> R: stop in a resumable way (open question)
E -> H: resumable stop of every affected session
H -> S: stop (goals are kept)
E -> B: goal revision per board:\nhandoff_ref = snapshot + note
E -> P: report: stopped, not stopped

== Later ==
P -> H: keeper up
H -> S: resume with the goal and its handoff note

caption Sources: spec §9, §11
@enduml
